Desktop and lockscreen widget positions relative to the output.

Widget positions (cx, cy) were absolute logical px, so a widget only stayed
in place at one logical output size: rotating the output or changing its
scale moved it, or pushed it off screen. They are now fractions of the
output's logical size, converted to px on placement; the widget editor
converts its snapshot to px on open and back on close. Desktop widgets also
get `desktopWidget.outputName()`, so that a plugin can size itself to its
output through `noctalia.outputs()`.

